# Scanwise server configuration.
# Local development: copy this file to .env.local and fill it in; `npm run dev` loads it.
# Production: add the same variables in Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables.

# OAuth web client ID for "Sign in with Google".
# Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials → Create credentials → OAuth client ID →
# Application type "Web application". Under "Authorized JavaScript origins" add:
#   http://localhost
#   http://localhost:3000
#   https://your-production-domain (e.g. https://scanwise.vercel.app)
# No redirect URIs are needed: sign-in uses the Google popup.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=759853700395-uukt9srdb05pka0j7djjulmkqc2hkfqv.apps.googleusercontent.com

# Gemini API key for analysis, chat and AI vision. Create one in Google AI Studio:
#   https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# Keep it server-side only; it is never sent to the browser.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Secret that signs session cookies. At least 32 characters. Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('base64url'))"
# Changing it signs everyone out. When empty during `npm run dev`, a temporary secret is used
# (sessions end when the dev server restarts); production refuses to sign anyone in without it.
SESSION_SECRET=

# Optional: the Gemini model id. Defaults to gemini-3.8-flash.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash

# ---- Optional: Add sources from Google Drive ----------------------------------------------------
# Needs GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID above too. In the same Google Cloud project:
#   1. APIs & Services → Library: enable "Google Picker API" and "Google Drive API".
#   2. Credentials → Create credentials → API key. Restrict it to those two APIs and, under
#      "Website restrictions", to your origins (http://localhost:3000, https://your-production-domain).
#   3. OAuth consent screen → Data access: add the scope .../auth/drive.file (access only to files the
#      person picks).
# Both values are sent to the browser; the key is safe to expose once restricted as above.
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# The project number (not the id): IAM & Admin → Settings → Project number.
# GOOGLE_APP_ID=

# ---- Optional: Add sources from OneDrive -------------------------------------------------------
# Azure portal → Microsoft Entra ID → App registrations → New registration:
#   - Supported account types: "Accounts in any organizational directory and personal Microsoft accounts".
#   - Redirect URI: platform "Single-page application", value http://localhost:3000/auth/microsoft.html
#     (add https://your-production-domain/auth/microsoft.html as well).
#   - API permissions: Microsoft Graph → Delegated → User.Read and Files.Read. For work or school accounts,
#     also SharePoint → Delegated → MyFiles.Read (and AllSites.Read to pick from shared libraries).
# Then copy the "Application (client) ID". It is public.
# MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=
